 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the civil service law, in relation to permitting employees of\nthe state to be excused from work to donate blood",
    "basePrintNo": "S907",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S907-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §159-c, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S907\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the civil service law, in relation to permitting employ-\nees of the state to be excused from work to donate blood\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to encourage greater participation in\nblood drives and increase the pool of actual blood donors by providing\ntime off for donation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nState employees, at the discretion of the employees' appointing authori-\nty, may take time off for the purpose of donating blood. They may take\nup to four hours per donation. The appointing authority may require that\nthe employee provide written substantiation from the donation center\nthat he/she actually donated blood during the excused absence.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe State of New York is currently in the midst of a blood shortage.\nAccording to reports, there is less than a day's supply of blood on hand\nat varying hospitals throughout the State. This problem has continually\ncropped up in recent years as there have been fewer donors over the last\ndecade. State government can help alleviate this problem by providing\nits employees with a motive to donate blood\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18- A.2462 - Referred to Ways and Means\n\n2015-16- A.1917 - Referred to Ways and Means\n\n2013-14- A.368 - Held for Consideration in Ways and Means\n\n2011-12- A.1590 - Referred to Ways and Means\n\n2009-10- A.1838 - Referred to Governmental Employees/ 5.1711- Referred\nto Civil Service and Pensions\n\n2007-08- A.3102-A - Referred to Governmental Operations/ Referenced\nChanged to Government Employees\n\n2005-06- A.1427-A - Referred to Governmental Operations! Referenced\nChanged to Government Employees\n\n2003-04- A.7936 - Referred to Ways and Means/ 5.3480- Referred to Over-\nsight and Government Operations\n\n2001-02- A.8900 - Referred to Government Operations/ 5.1414- Referred to\nOversight and Government Operations\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
